---
import DocsLayout from "@/layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="API overview"
  path="/api/api-overview"
  section="api"
  description="The tested public API contract for KoAkademy — base URL, authentication, and errors."
>
  <p>
    KoAkademy's API is <strong>beta</strong>. Only the routes listed in this
    reference are a documented integration surface. Anything else in the
    application is internal and may change without a public compatibility
    guarantee — in particular, KoAkademy does not publish a student CRUD API
    contract.
  </p>

  <h2>Endpoints</h2>

  <div class="api-endpoint">
    <div class="api-endpoint-header">
      <span class="api-method api-method-get">GET</span>
      <code class="api-endpoint-path">/api/v1/public/settings</code>
      <span class="api-status">Public · optional feature</span>
    </div>
    <div class="api-endpoint-body">
      <p>
        Selected public website settings for the institution. Requires the
        operator to enable the public API and the public-settings feature and to
        choose the allowed fields. See
        <a href="/api/authenticated-settings#public-website-settings"
          >Public website settings</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="api-endpoint">
    <div class="api-endpoint-header">
      <span class="api-method api-method-get">GET</span>
      <code class="api-endpoint-path">/api/settings</code>
      <span class="api-status">Sanctum</span>
    </div>
    <div class="api-endpoint-body">
      <p>
        Collection of general setting resources. Returns <code>404</code> when empty.
        See
        <a href="/api/authenticated-settings">Authenticated settings</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="api-endpoint">
    <div class="api-endpoint-header">
      <span class="api-method api-method-post">POST</span>
      <code class="api-endpoint-path">/api/students/verify</code>
      <span class="api-status">Sanctum</span>
    </div>
    <div class="api-endpoint-body">
      <p>
        Checks whether one student ID and email address match the same record.
        See
        <a href="/api/student-verification">Student verification</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Base URL</h2>
  <p>
    Use the configured application origin with <code>/api</code>, for example
    <code>https://school.example/api</code>. There is no shared KoAkademy API
    hostname — self-hosted installations serve their own API.
  </p>

  <h2>Authentication</h2>
  <p>
    Protected routes use Laravel Sanctum. Clients with a token provisioned by
    their operator send:
  </p>
  <pre><code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN
Accept: application/json</code></pre>
  <p>
    Token issuance and revocation are deployment responsibilities. No public
    token-creation endpoint is documented in this release. Never put tokens in
    source code, browser logs, URLs, or public issue reports.
  </p>

  <h2>Status codes</h2>
  <p>All requests and responses use JSON and normal HTTP status codes:</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Code</th>
        <th>Meaning</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td
          ><span class="api-status">200</span> · <span class="api-status"
            >201</span
          ></td
        >
        <td>Success. <code>201</code> is returned on creation.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="api-status">401</span></td>
        <td>Missing or invalid Sanctum authentication.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="api-status">403</span></td>
        <td>Authenticated but denied.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="api-status">404</span></td>
        <td>Resource missing or feature disabled.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><span class="api-status">422</span></td>
        <td>Validation failure, with an <code>errors</code> object.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Stability</h2>
  <p>
    Field-level compatibility is limited to the examples covered by endpoint
    tests. Pin the latest stable KoAkademy version and verify integrations in
    staging before upgrades.
  </p>
  <p>
    Continue with
    <a href="/api/authenticated-settings">Authenticated settings</a> or
    <a href="/api/student-verification">Student verification</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
